 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "style",
   "key": "style",
   "short": "Style",
   "title": "Choose a binding style",
   "hideInSummary": true,
   "text": [
    "Medieval bindings changed over the centuries. Each style has its own way of sewing, boarding and covering a book."
   ],
   "question": "Which style do you want to choose?",
   "options": [
    {
     "value": "carolingian",
     "label": "Carolingian",
     "disabled": "in preparation"
    },
    {
     "value": "romanesque",
     "label": "Romanesque"
    },
    {
     "value": "gothic",
     "label": "Gothic",
     "disabled": "in preparation"
    }
   ],
   "scene": "block"
  },
  {
   "id": "holes",
   "key": "holes",
   "short": "Sewing holes",
   "title": "Holes for the thread",
   "text": [
    "Your quires are stacked on top of one another. It is time to decide how many sewing supports you will bind the book with. This book block will be designed for three sewing supports, and they will be equally spaced, since that was the most common design.",
    "Since the supports will be sewn to the book block, the book block has to have holes in it for the thread. This was probably done while the quires were held tight in a press."
   ],
   "question": "Will the holes be cut in, as with a knife or chisel, or pierced, as with an awl or needle?",
   "options": [
    {
     "value": "cut",
     "label": "Cut"
    },
    {
     "value": "pierced",
     "label": "Pierced"
    }
   ],
   "scene": "block"
  },
  {
   "id": "endleaves",
   "key": "endleaves",
   "short": "Endleaves",
   "title": "Endleaves",
   "text": [
    "Now you have to decide whether to add endleaves. When included, these were additional wraps for the book block. Sometimes they were glued down to the inside cover, almost always after the book board had been covered with leather or another material."
   ],
   "question": "Will you:",
   "options": [
    {
     "value": "none",
     "label": "Use no endleaves"
    },
    {
     "value": "own",
     "label": "Use the first and last pages of the book block"
    },
    {
     "value": "quire",
     "label": "Add a thin additional quire"
    },
    {
     "value": "wrap",
     "label": "Wrap the whole book block in a large bifolium"
    }
   ],
   "after": [
    "The form could vary, particularly of the additional quire. Sometimes it was a folio with a stub. Finally, front and back endleaves could be treated differently."
   ],
   "scene": "block"
  },
  {
   "id": "support",
   "key": "support",
   "short": "Supports",
   "title": "Sewing supports",
   "text": [
    "The quires are now ready to be sewn together. They will be sewn together along three sewing supports, which will later be laced into the book boards. These sewing supports are made of alum-tawed leather and measured about 8–20 mm in width."
   ],
   "question": "Will you choose:",
   "options": [
    {
     "value": "slit",
