   "title": "Fastening",
   "text": [
    "Finally, a fastening could be fashioned. A leather strap, sewn together of two leather pieces, was generally used. It was nailed into the side near the free edge of one of the covers, generally the upper cover. An eyelet or hasp of bronze or iron was attached to the end. Sometimes it was decorated with geometric, floral or animal designs. It had a hole that fit around a peg on the opposite cover.",
